## ---------------------------------------------------------------- shadows

option.shadowMapResolution=Shadow Resolution
option.shadowMapResolution.comment=Size of the shadow map. Higher values resolve finer detail - window frames, handrails, bogies - at a real cost in performance and memory.

option.shadowDistance=Shadow Distance
option.shadowDistance.comment=How far from the camera shadows are drawn, in blocks. Long objects such as trains need a larger value than the terrain alone would.
suffix.shadowDistance=m

option.SHADOW_FILTER=Shadow Filter
option.SHADOW_FILTER.comment=How the shadow edge is softened.
value.SHADOW_FILTER.0=Hard
value.SHADOW_FILTER.1=Soft (PCF)
value.SHADOW_FILTER.2=Contact hardening
value.SHADOW_FILTER.3=Contact hardening (high)

option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS=Shadow Softness
option.SHADOW_SOFTNESS.comment=Width of the penumbra. The shadow stays sharp where an object touches the ground and spreads with distance, so this mostly affects overhangs and roofs.

option.SHADOW_DISTORTION=Shadow Distortion
option.SHADOW_DISTORTION.comment=Concentrates shadow map resolution near the camera. Higher values sharpen nearby shadows and coarsen distant ones. Lower it when you want an even quality across a long scene such as a station platform.

option.SHADOW_BIAS_SCALE=Shadow Bias
option.SHADOW_BIAS_SCALE.comment=Global offset applied before the shadow lookup. Raise it if surfaces show striping, lower it if shadows detach from what casts them.

option.SHADOW_BRIGHTNESS=Shadow Brightness
option.SHADOW_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Light level inside a shadow, on top of what the sky already contributes.

option.COLORED_SHADOWS=Coloured Shadows
option.COLORED_SHADOWS.comment=Light that passes through stained glass, ice or a tinted window keeps that colour instead of being blocked outright.

## --------------------------------------------------------------- entities

option.ENTITY_SHADOW_BIAS=Entity Shadow Bias
option.ENTITY_SHADOW_BIAS.comment=Extra shadow offset applied to entities only. Entity models are thin and often self-intersecting, which produces striping at a bias terrain is perfectly happy with. Raise this if a mob or vehicle shows dark bands across it.

option.entityShadowDistanceMul=Entity Shadow Range
option.entityShadowDistanceMul.comment=Multiplies the shadow distance for entities. Entities are culled by the distance of their origin, so a long entity - a train car, a ship - can lose its shadow while most of it is still in range. Raise this if shadows pop off long vehicles. Iris only.

option.HIDE_VANILLA_ENTITY_SHADOW=Hide Blob Shadow
option.HIDE_VANILLA_ENTITY_SHADOW.comment=Removes the flat oval the game paints under every entity. The shadow map already draws the entity's real silhouette; leaving both on puts a dark ellipse under an otherwise correct shadow.

option.ENTITY_SPECULAR=Entity Glossiness
option.ENTITY_SPECULAR.comment=How reflective entities are when the resource pack supplies no specular map.

option.VEHICLE_SPECULAR=Vehicle Glossiness
option.VEHICLE_SPECULAR.comment=Same, for entities listed as vehicles in entity.properties. Higher values read as lacquered paintwork.

## --------------------------------------------------------------- lighting

option.SUN_ILLUMINANCE=Sunlight
option.SUN_ILLUMINANCE.comment=Strength of direct light from the sun and moon.

option.SKY_ILLUMINANCE=Skylight
option.SKY_ILLUMINANCE.comment=Strength of ambient light gathered from the sky dome.

option.BLOCKLIGHT_INTENSITY=Block Light
option.BLOCKLIGHT_INTENSITY.comment=Strength of torches, lanterns and other light sources.

option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE=Block Light Colour
option.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE.comment=Colour temperature of block light. Low values are candle warm, high values are daylight white.
suffix.BLOCKLIGHT_TEMPERATURE=K

option.MINIMUM_LIGHT=Minimum Light
option.MINIMUM_LIGHT.comment=Floor on how dark an unlit surface can get.

option.ambientOcclusionLevel=Vanilla Ambient Occlusion
option.ambientOcclusionLevel.comment=How much of Minecraft's own baked corner shading is kept.

option.SPECULAR_HIGHLIGHT=Specular Highlights
option.SPECULAR_HIGHLIGHT.comment=Sun and sky reflections on surfaces. This is what puts the moving sheen along a vehicle's flank.

option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING=Subsurface Scattering
option.SUBSURFACE_SCATTERING.comment=Light passing through thin surfaces such as leaves and grass.

option.HANDHELD_LIGHT=Handheld Light
option.HANDHELD_LIGHT.comment=A carried torch or lantern lights the world around you.

option.SSAO=Ambient Occlusion
option.SSAO.comment=Darkens creases and contact points that the shadow map is too coarse to catch.

option.SSAO_SAMPLES=AO Samples
option.SSAO_SAMPLES.comment=Sample count for ambient occlusion.

option.SSAO_RADIUS=AO Radius
option.SSAO_RADIUS.comment=How far ambient occlusion reaches, in blocks.

option.SSAO_STRENGTH=AO Strength
option.SSAO_STRENGTH.comment=How dark ambient occlusion is allowed to get.

## ------------------------------------------------------------- atmosphere

option.sunPathRotation=Sun Path Angle
option.sunPathRotation.comment=Tilts the path the sun travels. Anything other than zero means the sun stops passing exactly overhead, which gives longer, more interesting shadows all day.
suffix.sunPathRotation=°

option.SKY_SATURATION=Sky Saturation
option.SKY_SATURATION.comment=Colour intensity of the sky.

option.FOG_DENSITY=Fog Density
option.FOG_DENSITY.comment=Thickness of the distance haze. Distant geometry fades towards the colour of the sky in that exact direction.

option.FOG_ALTITUDE_FALLOFF=Fog Height Falloff
option.FOG_ALTITUDE_FALLOFF.comment=How quickly fog thins out with altitude. Higher values keep haze in the valleys and clear the peaks.

option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT=Light Shafts
option.VOLUMETRIC_LIGHT.comment=Sunbeams through the air, sampled from the same shadow map as the surfaces - so they line up with what actually casts them.

option.VOLUMETRIC_STEPS=Light Shaft Quality
option.VOLUMETRIC_STEPS.comment=Ray marching steps. More steps means smoother shafts.

option.VOLUMETRIC_STRENGTH=Light Shaft Strength
option.VOLUMETRIC_STRENGTH.comment=Brightness of the light shafts.

option.CLOUD_BRIGHTNESS=Cloud Brightness
option.CLOUD_BRIGHTNESS.comment=Brightness of Minecraft's clouds.

## ------------------------------------------------------------------ water

option.WATER_WAVES=Water Waves
option.WATER_WAVES.comment=Animated surface displacement on water, matched in the shadow pass.

option.WATER_WAVE_HEIGHT=Wave Height
option.WATER_WAVE_HEIGHT.comment=Size of the water waves.

option.WATER_REFLECTIONS=Water Reflections
option.WATER_REFLECTIONS.comment=Reflections on the water surface.

option.REFRACTION=Refraction
option.REFRACTION.comment=Bends what is seen through water and glass.

option.WATER_ABSORPTION=Water Absorption
option.WATER_ABSORPTION.comment=How quickly water swallows light. Higher values make deep water darker and greener.

option.WATER_ALPHA=Water Tint
option.WATER_ALPHA.comment=How strongly the biome's water colour tints what is seen through the surface.

option.SSR=Screen Space Reflections
option.SSR.comment=Reflects the scene on the screen, falling back to the sky for anything off-camera.

option.SSR_STEPS=Reflection Quality
option.SSR_STEPS.comment=Ray marching steps for screen space reflections.

option.SSR_REFINE=Reflection Refinement
option.SSR_REFINE.comment=Binary search steps used to land the reflection on the surface rather than past it.

## ----------------------------------------------------------------- waving

option.WAVING_PLANTS=Waving Plants
option.WAVING_PLANTS.comment=Grass, flowers and crops bend in the wind.

option.WAVING_LEAVES=Waving Leaves
option.WAVING_LEAVES.comment=Leaf blocks sway in the wind.

option.WAVING_STRENGTH=Wind Strength
option.WAVING_STRENGTH.comment=How far foliage is displaced.

## ------------------------------------------------------------------- post

option.TONEMAP=Tone Curve
option.TONEMAP.comment=How high dynamic range light is fitted onto the display.
value.TONEMAP.0=Reinhard
value.TONEMAP.1=ACES
value.TONEMAP.2=Filmic
value.TONEMAP.3=AgX

option.AUTO_EXPOSURE=Auto Exposure
option.AUTO_EXPOSURE.comment=Adapts brightness to the scene, the way an eye does on stepping out of a tunnel.

option.EXPOSURE_SPEED=Adaptation Speed
option.EXPOSURE_SPEED.comment=How quickly auto exposure reacts.

option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE=Exposure
option.MANUAL_EXPOSURE.comment=Overall brightness multiplier, applied on top of auto exposure.

option.WHITE_BALANCE=White Balance
option.WHITE_BALANCE.comment=Colour temperature the image is neutralised to. Below 6500 K cools the picture, above warms it.
suffix.WHITE_BALANCE=K

option.VIBRANCE=Vibrance
option.VIBRANCE.comment=Lifts muted colours while leaving already saturated ones alone.

option.SATURATION=Saturation
option.SATURATION.comment=Overall colour intensity.

option.CONTRAST=Contrast
option.CONTRAST.comment=Separation between the darks and the brights.

option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH=Vignette
option.VIGNETTE_STRENGTH.comment=Darkening towards the corners of the frame.

option.BLOOM=Bloom
option.BLOOM.comment=Glare around bright areas.

option.BLOOM_STRENGTH=Bloom Strength
option.BLOOM_STRENGTH.comment=How much glare is mixed back into the image.

option.TAA=Temporal Anti-Aliasing
option.TAA.comment=Smooths edges and resolves the sampling noise in soft shadows and ambient occlusion by accumulating across frames. Turning it off makes that noise visible as a fixed dither pattern.

option.TAA_SHARPEN=TAA Sharpening
option.TAA_SHARPEN.comment=Compensates for the softening that temporal accumulation introduces.

option.SHARPEN=Sharpening
option.SHARPEN.comment=Extra edge definition applied to the final image.
